  "body": "**Replaces #439**, which was opened from the old fork. GitHub detached that fork from this repo's network when NeoTech/Camcraft was briefly private, so #439 can no longer be updated. This branch carries the merges with main through #461; the conflicts were with #444 (MCP post files), #382 (machine module list), #451 (sticky refusal) and #400 (detect_holes moved to the app; the per-setup radial reading moved with it).\n\nFollow-up to #343 (per-setup machine and post).\n\n## What changed\n**Generation.** Every machine reader now takes the operation's own setup, so an inactive setup's ops generate against their own machine. The \"activate 'SetupN' first\" refusal is retired. A setup's machine is parsed, or refused by name, when it's mounted or when the document opens, so no replacement refusal is needed.\n\n**Readers switched to the op's (or setup's) own mount:**\n- generation (`job.rs`): machine kind, `is_mill`, spindle housing, rotaries;\n- `spindle_law::turns(world, setup, params)`. As a side effect, activating a setup no longer changes any op's stamp;\n- `rest::prior_plan`'s lathe rule;\n- `setup_align::generation_problem`;\n- `stock_sim_carry::carry_turn`, which now requires both ends to be mills;\n- fixtures: the table, `boxes_for`, `workholding_for` and `list`;\n- the gate's spindle-housing, limit and inverted-axis checks, each per machine;\n- the op-family gate for paste and retype;\n- UI: retype rows and the drill radial-holes reading.\n\nThe readers that stay on the active mount (the ribbon, the Setup/Machine/Post pages, the new-op door, display-only clocks) are listed with reasons in `docs/decisions/388-per-setup-mount.md`.\n\n**Posting.** A program over several machines or posts writes **one NC file per mount** (new `posting_mounts.rs`: `post_mounts` / `post_mounts_script`).\n- Setups that share both machine and post share a file, named `<stem>_<nn>_<setups>.<ext>` with each post's own extension.\n- The gate runs once over the whole program, with each op judged on its own machine. Each file adds its own work-offset register check.\n- Nothing is written unless every file passes.\n- The \"one program is written by one post for one machine\" clause is retired.\n- The UI, `cam.post`, MCP `post` and CLI `process -o` all route through it. A single file returns the same JSON as before; several files add `files` and `mounts`. `cam.d.ts` is updated.\n- Per-op files post each op through its own setup's post.\n\n**Posted output changes only for programs over more than one mount** (refused before). Single-mount output is byte-identical, and every existing golden and posting suite passes. One edge case: an active setup with its own mount but no ops, while the ops are on another mount, used to be refused and now posts on the ops' mount.\n\n## How tested\n- New `setup_mounts_post` (5 tests):\n  - an inactive setup generates on its own machine, mill + lathe in both directions, with stamps fresh across activation;\n  - a mill and a lathe post as two files, each byte-identical to posting that setup alone;\n  - a travel limit is judged on the op's own machine only, whichever setup is active;\n  - per-op files use each op's own post;\n  - the script (CLI/MCP) path writes the same files.\n- `setup_mount` (6): both old refusal tests are replaced by tests proving the new behaviour.\n- After merging main at #412: `setup_mounts_post`, `setup_mount`, `fixtures` and `posting` pass. `clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --tests -D warnings` is clean.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick` passes except tests already red on main: #415 and the headless-GPU ui tests.\n\n## Not exercised / follow-ups\n- The tool-number clash (#221) is still judged over the whole program, which over-refuses across machines: #438.\n- No real-machine run of the multi-file output, though each file equals its setup posted alone.\n\nChangelog: Setups on different machines or posts: inactive setups generate on their own machine; the post writes one NC file per machine/post, each judged against its own machine (#388)\n\nFixes #388\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
